  {
   "id": "uBTkrfOmNrsJ",
   "from": "Bob Carpenter",
   "author": "8aa9b8cc06fdc99c",
   "date": "2013-03-29T18:51:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] weird clang++ error",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "clang++ still works OK on our macs.  But it could\r<br>easily work differently under linux.  I believe what\r<br>is happening is that some of the old c lib functions\r<br>get automatically brought into global scope on some\r<br>platforms.  We&#39;re not explicitly qualifying them so as\r<br>to use argument-dependent lookup where we need to for\r<br>our auto-diff vars.\r<br>\r<br>We just need to add explicit using statements in the\r<br>scopes where fabs gets used (NOT namespace scope -- restrict\r<br>as locally as possible within a function).\r<br>\r<br>We only tracked this down because of the weird behavior we were\r<br>getting from lgamma at one point.\r<br>\r<br>- Bob\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On 3/29/13 2:08 PM, Ben Goodrich wrote:\r<br>&gt; Doing test-unit with clang++ (only), I immediately get\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt; clang++ -I src -I lib/eigen_3.1.2 -I lib/boost_1.53.0 -Wall -DBOOST_RESULT_OF_USE_TR1 -DBOOST_NO_DECLTYPE\r<br>&gt; -DBOOST_DISABLE_ASSERTS -Wno-unused-function -Wno-uninitialized   -c -O3 -DGTEST_HAS_PTHREAD=0 -I\r<br>&gt; lib/gtest_1.6.0/include -I lib/gtest_1.6.0 lib/gtest_1.6.0/src/gtest-all.cc -o test/gtest.o\r<br>&gt; In file included from lib/gtest_1.6.0/src/gtest-all.cc:42:\r<br>&gt; In file included from lib/gtest_1.6.0/src/gtest.cc:132:\r<br>&gt; lib/gtest_1.6.0/src/gtest-internal-inl.h:206:8: warning: private field &#39;pretty_&#39; is not used [-Wunused-private-field]\r<br>&gt;    bool pretty_;\r<br>&gt;         ^\r<br>&gt; fatal error: error in backend: Cannot select: 0x508a070: i64 = fabs 0x5074840 [ORD=532] [ID=31]\r<br>&gt;    0x5074840: i64 = zero_extend 0x5074940 [ID=30]\r<br>&gt;      0x5074940: i8 = X86ISD::SETCC 0x5089970, 0x541b400:1 [ID=28]\r<br>&gt;        0x5089970: i8 = Constant&lt;9&gt; [ID=15]\r<br>&gt;        0x541b400: i64,i32 = X86ISD::SUB 0x541b000, 0x5074b40 [ID=26]\r<br>&gt;          0x541b000: i64 = add 0x541b200, 0x5363500 [ORD=528] [ID=24]\r<br>&gt;            0x541b200: i64,ch = load 0x541b100, 0x5363700, 0x541a800&lt;LD8[%149](tbaa=!&quot;any pointer&quot;)&gt; [ORD=527] [ID=22]\r<br>&gt;              0x5363700: i64 = FrameIndex&lt;7&gt; [ORD=522] [ID=1]\r<br>&gt;              0x541a800: i64 = undef [ORD=526] [ID=7]\r<br>&gt;            0x5363500: i64 = Constant&lt;-24&gt; [ORD=528] [ID=10]\r<br>&gt;          0x5074b40: i64 = X86ISD::Wrapper 0x5089670 [ID=19]\r<br>&gt;            0x5089670: i64 = TargetGlobalAddress&lt;[0 x i64]* @_ZNSs4_Rep20_S_empty_rep_storageE&gt; 0 [ID=16]\r<br>&gt; In function: _ZN7testing8UnitTest17AddTestPartResultENS_14TestPartResult4TypeEPKciRKNS_8internal6StringES8_\r<br>&gt; make: *** [test/gtest.o] Error 1\r<br>&gt; |\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Is anyone else seeing this?\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Ben\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; --\r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;stan development mailing list&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-dev+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.\r<br>&gt; For more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477021011000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1lRujjolmLfgJsG8GvwHDw\">https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out</a>.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
