  {
   "id": "ne25K33mWqgJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2013-03-29T19:47:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] weird clang++ error",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Friday, March 29, 2013 2:51:49 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">clang++ still works OK on our macs.  But it could\r\n<br>easily work differently under linux.  I believe what\r\n<br>is happening is that some of the old c lib functions\r\n<br>get automatically brought into global scope on some\r\n<br>platforms.  We&#39;re not explicitly qualifying them so as\r\n<br>to use argument-dependent lookup where we need to for\r\n<br>our auto-diff vars.\r\n<br></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><br>That might be part of the story, but I also found a similar Debian bugreport for clang 3.2 that seems to be triggered when someone upgrades to g++-4.8 and libc 2.17 (and thus changes some of the underlying libraries). Also, the error message refers to a string<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><code><span style=\"color:#606\"><span style=\"color:#606\">In</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span></span><span style=\"color:#008\"><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><span style=\"color:#000\"> _</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ZN7testing8UnitTest17AddTestPa</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rtResultENS_</span><span style=\"color:#000\">14TestPartResult4TypeEPKciRKNS</span><span style=\"color:#000\">_8internal6StringES8_</span></span></code></div></code></div><br>so I don&#39;t know how fabs would get involved. Anyway, the problem probably has more to do with my setup than with Stan.<br><br>Ben<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "F9dtkJACpVwJ",
   "from": "Jiqiang Guo",
