   "subject": "Re: [stan-dev] weird clang++ error",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Just to report that I do not have this problem for clang 3.0 (I do not know to upgrade to 3.2 on linux easily):<div><br></div><div><div>$ clang -v</div><div>Debian clang version 3.0-6.1 (tags/RELEASE_30/final) (based on LLVM 3.0)</div>\r\n<div>Target: x86_64-pc-linux-gnu</div><div>Thread model: posix</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>In addition, that long function&#39;s real names is:</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div>$ c++filt _ZN7testing8UnitTest17AddTestPartResultENS_14TestPartResult4TypeEPKciRKNS_8internal6StringES8_</div>\r\n<div>testing::UnitTest::AddTestPartResult(testing::TestPartResult::Type, char const*, int, testing::internal::String const&amp;, testing::internal::String const&amp;)</div></div><div><br></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\">\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Fri, Mar 29, 2013 at 3:47 PM, Ben Goodrich <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">goodri...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div>On Friday, March 29, 2013 2:51:49 PM UTC-4, Bob Carpenter wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">clang++ still works OK on our macs.  But it could\r\n<br>easily work differently under linux.  I believe what\r\n<br>is happening is that some of the old c lib functions\r\n<br>get automatically brought into global scope on some\r\n<br>platforms.  We&#39;re not explicitly qualifying them so as\r\n<br>to use argument-dependent lookup where we need to for\r\n<br>our auto-diff vars.\r\n<br></blockquote></div><div><br>That might be part of the story, but I also found a similar Debian bugreport for clang 3.2 that seems to be triggered when someone upgrades to g++-4.8 and libc 2.17 (and thus changes some of the underlying libraries). Also, the error message refers to a string<br>\r\n<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><code><span style=\"color:#606\"><span style=\"color:#606\">In</span></span><span><span> </span></span><span style=\"color:#008\"><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span></span><span><span> _</span><u></u><span>ZN7testing8UnitTest17AddTestPa</span><u></u><span>rtResultENS_</span><u></u><span>14TestPartResult4TypeEPKciRKNS</span><u></u><span>_8internal6StringES8_</span></span></code></div>\r\n</code></div><br>so I don&#39;t know how fabs would get involved. Anyway, the problem probably has more to do with my setup than with Stan.<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br><br>Ben<br><br></font></span></div>\r\n</blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;stan development mailing list&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">stan-dev+u...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792477021014000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1JRozsgb6VR4vzYbe32e4e\">https://groups.google.com/groups/opt_out</a>.<br>\r\n <br>\r\n <br>\r\n</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
